<ProseLayout
  title="Disclosures: sponsored listings and partner links"
  description="How NewsMap labels sponsored listings and partner links, and why payment never changes an outlet's editorial position."
  heading="Sponsored listings and partner links"
  updated="2026-10-27"
>
  <p>NewsMap earns money in two ways. Neither changes the order in which outlets are ranked.</p>

  <h2>Sponsored listings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Outlets can pay to appear in up to three sponsored places at the top of a category in a
      country.
    </li>
    <li>
      Sponsored places carry the word Sponsored and a highlighted background, and sit above the
      editorial ranking, separated from it.
    </li>
    <li>
      Every sponsored listing is reviewed by an editor before it goes live. We refuse sites that are
      not news outlets or that mislead readers, and refund them.
    </li>
    <li>
      Links in sponsored places are marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code> for search engines.
    </li>
    <li>
      Click figures we give sponsors are labeled as filtered estimates: we remove automated traffic
      and repeated clicks, and some browsers block our counting.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Partner links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Some pages show one partner offer, such as a VPN for reading on public Wi-Fi or a service that
      sells legitimate access to paid newspapers.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you buy through a partner link, we may earn a commission. The offer is labeled as a partner
      link where it appears.
    </li>
    <li>
      We never promote tools for getting around paywalls, broadcasting rights or a site's terms of
      use.
    </li>
    <li>
      VPN offers are not shown to visitors from countries where VPN use is banned or restricted.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    The site does not show display advertising today. If that changes, ads will be labeled, kept
    away from the ranking, and loaded only after you give consent where the law requires it. This
    page will be updated first.
  </p>
</ProseLayout>
